@title Customer Advisory Council charter
@subtitle Windrow Software, effective 2027-01-01, sponsored by Ines Carvalho, Chief Product Officer

## Purpose

The council gives customers a structured, regular way to shape the product roadmap, and to tell us plainly what is not working.

## Membership

- The council has 14 seats: 12 customers and 2 Windrow product leads.
- Customer seats are chosen to reflect our customer base by size and industry.
- Customer members serve two-year terms, renewable once.
- Half the customer seats rotate each year, to keep continuity.
- The chair is Ines Carvalho. The vice chair is elected by the customer members.

## Meetings

- Quarterly, for two hours, on 2027-03-10, 2027-06-09, 2027-09-08 and 2027-12-08.
- The agenda is sent 10 days ahead.
- Written minutes are shared within 5 business days.
- A quorum is 8 members, including at least 6 customers.

## What the council does and does not do

The council reviews roadmap themes, tests early designs, and ranks customer-submitted requests.

It does not approve pricing. It cannot commit Windrow to a delivery date. It does not replace the normal support channel.

## Confidentiality

All members sign a mutual NDA before the first meeting. Roadmap material shown to the council is confidential unless marked otherwise.
